    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.24.1 release assets and hashed independently. v5.24.0 made a DARQ install behave like a Pegasus one by filling the notifier plugin's orchestrator name from the content-declared name instead of a hardcoded literal. v5.24.1 corrects a cosmetic defect that shipped with it: the comment explaining the mechanism named the placeholders it described, so substitution -- which runs over an asset's whole text, comments included -- rewrote the comment itself, leaving nonsense prose and the installing machine's absolute skills path inside a shipped plugin. Only the `pegasus` artifact changed; install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.23.0."
